EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for your interest in Arizona State University. I have included some information below to help you with the transfer process.

You can review our transfer admission requirements online at https://transfer.asu.edu/transferrequirements. Some majors have additional requirements, which can be viewed by searching for your major on degree search.

To transfer to ASU, your first step is to apply for admission at https://transfer.asu.edu/apply and pay the application fee online. After you have submitted your application, contact your high school and all colleges you have previously attended to request official transcripts be sent directly to ASU Admission Services. ASU requires an official high school transcript if you have not completed an associate degree or bachelor's degree at the time you apply. Once we receive all materials, your file will be reviewed for admission. The review process may take up to 4 – 6 weeks.

After you apply to ASU, you will receive an email and a letter containing your ASURITE UserID and activation code. Follow the instructions to activate your My ASU account at https://my.asu/edu. You will be able to track your admission status on My ASU.

Once admitted to ASU, you must meet with an academic advisor in your major and submit MMR immunization records to our student health office, prior to registering for classes. Instructions for these and other next steps can be found at https://transfer.asu.edu/steps, including how to get your ASU ID card, apply for financial aid and scholarships, purchase a parking permit, pay tuition and more.

If you have any questions, let me know and I will be happy to help.

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

